sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant GW as External Gateway<br/>Kuadrant/Authorino<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant API as batch-gateway-apiserver<br/>8000/TCP HTTP(S)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>TCP
    participant S3 as S3-Compatible Storage<br/>HTTP(S)
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>TCP
    participant Proc as batch-gateway-processor<br/>StatefulSet
    participant LLMd as llm-d Inference Gateway<br/>HTTP(S)
    participant GC as batch-gateway-gc
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over Client,LLMd: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission and Processing

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/files<br/>HTTPS, Auth (API key/token)
    GW->>API: Forward + X-MaaS-Username header<br/>HTTP(S)/8000
    API->>PG: Store file metadata<br/>TCP, Connection URL creds
    API->>S3: Upload input JSONL file<br/>HTTP(S), AWS credentials
    API-->>GW: File ID response
    GW-->>Client: File ID

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/batches<br/>HTTPS, Auth (API key/token)
    GW->>API: Forward + X-MaaS-Username header<br/>HTTP(S)/8000
    API->>PG: Create batch job record<br/>TCP, Connection URL creds
    API->>Redis: Enqueue job to priority queue<br/>TCP, Connection URL creds
    API-->>GW: Batch ID response
    GW-->>Client: Batch ID

    loop Poll Queue (every 5s)
        Proc->>Redis: Dequeue job<br/>TCP, Connection URL creds
    end

    Proc->>PG: Update job status → in_progress<br/>TCP
    Proc->>S3: Download input file<br/>HTTP(S), AWS credentials

    loop Per-model execution plan
        Proc->>LLMd: POST inference request<br/>HTTP(S), Optional API key/mTLS
        Note over Proc,LLMd: AIMD concurrency control<br/>global: 100, per-endpoint: 10<br/>Backs off on 429/5xx
        LLMd-->>Proc: Inference response
    end

    Proc->>S3: Upload output file<br/>HTTP(S), AWS credentials
    Proc->>PG: Update job status → completed<br/>TCP

    Client->>GW: GET /v1/batches/{batch_id}<br/>HTTPS
    GW->>API: Forward<br/>HTTP(S)/8000
    API->>PG: Query job status<br/>TCP
    API-->>GW: Job status + output_file_id
    GW-->>Client: Status response

    Client->>GW: GET /v1/files/{file_id}/content<br/>HTTPS
    GW->>API: Forward<br/>HTTP(S)/8000
    API->>S3: Download output file<br/>HTTP(S)
    API-->>GW: File content stream
    GW-->>Client: JSONL results

    Note over GC,K8s: Flow 2: Garbage Collection & Orphan Reconciliation

    loop Every 30m
        GC->>PG: Scan for expired jobs/files<br/>TCP
        GC->>S3: Delete expired files<br/>HTTP(S), AWS credentials
        GC->>PG: Mark jobs/files as deleted<br/>TCP
    end

    loop Every 60m (Orphan Reconciler)
        GC->>K8s: Watch processor pods<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
        Note over GC,K8s: Detect crashed processors<br/>via pod status
        GC->>PG: Check in-flight jobs for dead processors<br/>TCP
        GC->>Redis: Re-enqueue stuck jobs (CAS)<br/>TCP
        GC->>PG: Or expire if unrecoverable<br/>TCP
    end
